<title>UK: BP Chemicals investing 35 mln stg in Scotland.</title>
<headline>BP Chemicals investing 35 mln stg in Scotland.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>BP Chemicals, a division of British Petroleum Plc, on Wednesday announced a 35 million stg project to expand capacity of its G4 ethylene cracker plant at Grangemouth in Scotland.</p>
<p>The investment will increase capacity by 50,000 tonnes to 320,000 tonnes. Work starts immediately and will take 17 months, creating 150 jobs at its peak, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717.</p>
</text>
